  "body": "## What changed\n\nThe simulation's stock body was never visible in v0.23.0 (#2396).\n\n**Cause.** #2181 (the stock removal calculated before playback) moved the playback worker's `PackedBase::of` call after the calculation. The calculation leaves the playback at the end of the program. `PackedBase::of` runs the eikonal pass, which writes `max(mesh, cut)` into the mesh layer, and later frames can only lift cells over it. So the GPU eye's base was the **finished** part, and every frame at every playhead drew the finished part. When a program machines the part to size, that body sits inside the model, so no stock is seen.\n\n**Fix.** `crates/app/src/stock_play_worker.rs`: the base is packed from the uncut stock before the calculation runs, as it was before #2181. This is a one-line move with a comment. Decision record: `docs/decisions/2396-sim-stock-visible.md`.\n\n## How tested\n\n- Pinning test `crates/app/tests/stock_play_precalc.rs::the_picture_at_the_start_is_the_uncut_stock_after_the_calculation`. It spawns the worker with the calculation, waits for `Ready` and takes the packed frame at move 0. It asserts that the composed lattice the eye draws (`max(base.mesh, cut) < 0`) holds the uncut stock's material, and that the base mesh layer is the uncut stock's bit for bit.\n  - Before the fix: FAILED, `move 0 draws the uncut stock, not the finished part`, left 2016 (the finished part's texels), right 2880 (the uncut stock's).\n  - After the fix: ok.\n- The whole `stock_play_precalc` suite passes (8 pass, 1 heavy lane ignored).\n- `cargo xtask gate quick --base upstream/main` on head 4481c2a06: green (app lib, stock_play, stock_play_partial, stock_play_precalc; 5 steps, 0 failed).\n- `cargo clippy -p camcraft-app --all-targets -- -D warnings`: clean.\n\n## Not exercised\n\n- The windowed app on a GPU. The test reads the packed lattice the GPU eye uploads, not pixels, so the shader composite is not run.\n- The maintainer's own project. The fixture is the #2181 suite's staged face with a part cube, where the finished stock equals the part.\n- No pixel snapshots were run or changed.\n\nChangelog: Simulation draws the stock body again: playback started from the finished part, hidden inside the model, after the removal was calculated before playback (#2396)\n\nEffort: high (no escalation)\n\nFixes #2396\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nhttps://claude.ai/code/session_01CUsqDAAAJyAPrC37zBzbbX\n",
